 ## Data Expectations
 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Threshold Checks (CI Gating)
+- `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` object: `{ metric_id: min_score }`.
+- A threshold passes if the metric's score is >= the minimum; null scores fail.
+- Reports gain top-level `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array) fields.
+- JSON reports include threshold details: `{ metric, min, score, passed }` per threshold.
+- Markdown reports add a "Thresholds" section showing PASS/FAIL status.
+- CLI `--threshold` flag (repeatable) parses as `metric=min`, validates range [0–1] and metric IDs, exits with code 2 on error.
+- Exit 1 if any threshold fails; 0 if all pass or no thresholds specified.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
+- `generateReport` threshold validation works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
